> Yes, a pick-axe or a unicorn horn. This doesn't make the unicorn
> horn more effective except when you use it as a weapon, and I don't
> remember whether it makes the pick-axe more effective to dig with

Well it seems it can be used to save a turn or two. From dig.c:

| digging.effort += 10 + rn2(5) + abon() +
|                 uwep->spe - greatest_erosion(uwep) + u.udaminc;
| if (Race_if(PM_DWARF))
|         digging.effort *= 2;

rn2(x) = random number from 0 to x-1
abon() = DEX and STR bonus as for attacks
uwep->spe = enchantment
u.udaminc = intrinsic damage

A quantity of "effort" needs to be accumulated before a successful
dig, the greater the above sum, the faster this will happen.
(Interestingly, if you are a dwarf the effort is doubled, including
the enchantment bonus.)

